  "name": "CRR_National_Indicators",
  "title": "CRR national indicators: red flags, ACC redirect and demographics",
  "status": "draft",
  "date": "2026-09-06",
  "publisher": "Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora - Community Referred Radiology Programme",
  "description": "The national Questionnaire. Every assessment answers this alongside the Questionnaire(s) of the selected exam/site bundle(s); the national library CRR_RedFlags evaluates it before any exam library (AD-03). It carries every redflag.* and funding.acc* indicator in the national vocabulary, the patient.* demographics, and the seven symptom.*/lab.* indicators that CRR_RedFlags composes as qualifiers of a compound flag (AD-14) - without those seven, RF-03, RF-12, RF-19, RF-20, RF-23 and RF-24 could never fire from a note. Item text and type are reproduced from vocabulary/indicators.json v1.0.0 and are not authored here. A compound red flag nests its redflag.* qualifiers under its stem; a qualifier belonging to another vocabulary group stays in that group so no linkId appears twice, and the authoritative composition is always the CQL, not this nesting. `prefix` is the RF id from the vocabulary. NOT CLINICALLY REVIEWED - inherits the review state of the vocabulary and of CRR_RedFlags.cql.",
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/cqf-library",
      "valueCanonical": "http://crr.health.nz/fhir/Library/CRR_RedFlags"
    }
  ],
